  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Two is \\(10\\%\\) of \\(x\\) and \\(20\\%\\) of \\(y.\\) What is \\(x - y?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "To recover a whole from a known percentage of it, divide the given part by that percentage. Since \\(10\\%=\\frac1{10}\\) and \\(20\\%=\\frac15\\),\n\\[\nx=2\\div\\frac1{10}=20,\\qquad y=2\\div\\frac15=10.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(x-y=20-10=\\boxed{10}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
